ROOT CAUSE (independent probe, not a pytest problem)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Probe: backend\.venv\Scripts\python.exe D:\jbcode\.probe\h60-fs-probe.py
base  = D:\jbcode\.probe\h60bt-r6-fresh (created by the pytest run itself)

Output (verbatim):
  exists: True isdir: True
  iterdir FAILED: PermissionError [WinError 5] ... '\h60bt-r6-fresh'
  chmod FAILED: PermissionError [WinError 5] ... '\h60bt-r6-fresh'
  mkdir+write FAILED: PermissionError [WinError 5] ... '\h60bt-r6-fresh\sub'
  rmtree FAILED: FileNotFoundError [WinError 3] ... '\h60bt-r6-fresh\sub'
  rmdir base FAILED: PermissionError [WinError 5] ... '\h60bt-r6-fresh'

Interpretation: Python's os.listdir / mkdir / chmod / rmdir are denied inside the
workspace temp area, while PowerShell (New-Item, Remove-Item, Out-File) succeeded
there in the same session. pytest's tmpdir plugin must list/clean/chmod its
basetemp on both startup and sessionfinish
(_pytest/tmpdir.py ensure_relative_to_basetemp + cleanup_dead_symlinks), so no
pytest run using tmp_path/tmp_path_factory can execute under this confinement.
The eight Z57 tests all require tmp_path (jobs_db / matching_db fixtures).

CONSEQUENCE: this is an environment block, NOT a product defect. No Z57 test
passed or failed on its merits here; the runtime behaviour of the reviewed
paging code remains UNVERIFIED by this review.

